{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The test leads and heat shrink fit the practical steps around my breadboards, relay module, and wiring supplies: testing temporary connections and insulating finished joints.",
    "The digital caliper feels useful because measuring small parts and checking fit supports both my electronics assembly and occasional hardware work."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The magnets, magnetic hooks, feeler gauge, and T-nuts require specific mounting, gap-measuring, or woodworking tasks that I do not currently have.",
    "The thermal camera relates to my infrared thermometer, but I have no current need for the added capability and do not know whether it fits my phone. Electronic cleaner likewise addresses a maintenance need I have not expressed."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in electronics seems to have been stretched into an interest in any electrical testing or maintenance product, even when it serves a different task.",
    "My caster and fastener purchases seem to have been taken as broad interest in hardware, without enough connection to a particular project or required dimensions."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I am more interested in supplies that help connect, assemble, insulate, or measure the components I have used than in tools that require a new task to justify them.",
    "Both heat shrink kits fit my needs, but they fill the same role, so I would choose only one. A close match does not mean I need another version of it."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my hands-on electronics interests but stretched them into tools and hardware without a clear current use."
}"}
